course: dictionary
lesson: 10282
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. «An osprey carries the fish head forward like a torpedo.» Ospreys are not weapons, so the clue is like a torpedo: the fish head is long, narrow and built to cut through the water.
explain: «On land penguins waddle like clumsy toys, but the moment they dive they shoot through the water like torpedoes.» Clumsy toys is slow and awkward, and shoot is fast, so torpedoes must mean something that moves very quickly and smoothly underwater.
explain: Torpedo can also be a doing word. To torpedo a plan means to ruin it completely. If someone says their plan was torpedoed, try the swap: did the plan fail? Then the meaning fits.
fact: A torpedo is a long, cigar-shaped weapon that moves underwater by itself and explodes when it hits a ship.
fact: To torpedo a ship means to hit it with a torpedo.
fact: To torpedo a plan (informal) means to ruin it completely.
fact: A torpedo ray is a fish that can give an electric shock.
fact: Torpedoes were used in both World Wars, including by submarines against ships such as the Lusitania.
exercise: «An osprey carries the fish head forward like a torpedo.» What is a torpedo like here? | A soft, round ball | A heavy, slow boat | A bird's nest | *A long, narrow shape that moves smoothly and fast
exercise: Our school trip plan was torpedoed when the bus broke down. What does torpedoed mean? | Made bigger | Sent to the bus station | *Ruined completely | Painted red
exercise: «The submarine fired a torpedo at the ship.» What is a torpedo in this sentence? | A type of food | A loud siren | A fish that gives shocks | *A weapon that moves underwater and explodes on hitting a ship
test: «Penguins shoot through the water like torpedoes.» What does this tell you? | They are swimming slowly | They are stuck and cannot move | They are sleeping on the ice | *They swim very fast and straight
test: What does it mean to torpedo a ship? | To count its sailors | To paint it | To sail slowly past it | *To hit it with a torpedo
exam: Lena says a torpedo ray is a kind of weapon. What is the correct meaning? | A submarine with a crew | A plant that grows in the sea | A type of ship | *A fish that can give an electric shock
